# Migration ordering

Do not apply any migration, schema change, or SQL that creates or replaces database objects on a live Supabase project — including `apply_migration` and `execute_sql` that mutates schema — until `npm run preflight:migration` exits 0.

That script refuses when the migration is uncommitted, when `HEAD` is ahead of the remote, or when no passing `Verify MVP` run exists for this exact commit.

A database ahead of committed code cannot be explained, reviewed or rebuilt. Four commits sat unpushed while their migrations were applied live; V1 drifted the same way from the other direction. This is a gate, not a preference.

A push starts `Verify MVP`. Wait for that run to pass for this exact commit; a push that has not finished is not a pass.
